@startuml activity-speaker-notes-decision
'' PlantUML over Mermaid because the notes decision is an ordered rule chain (first match wins) whose steps belong to
'' two owners and two moments — the pure model at the first paint, and the background reader after it — and whose
'' outcomes must be read off where each theorem of docs/theory/12 applies. Activity swimlanes show the owner of each
'' step, the vertical `elseif` chain renders the rules in their exact order (notes.cljs `plan`), `switch` renders the
'' three kinds of background work (evidence.cljs `settle`), and the SVG renders byte-reproducibly (README §4).
'' Lanes and fills, from the shared palette: orange = the pure, process-agnostic model (vinary.slides.notes), the
'' "model orange" of the pure libraries; teal = the renderer reading page text through pdf.js
'' (vinary.slides.evidence). The red notes mark the two paths that can hide a slide with no CONFIRM to catch it.
!include _vv-theme.iuml
!pragma useVerticalIf on

title Where a Beamer deck's note pages are decided — ADR-0048 §2, proved in theory/12

|#F5EAE0|pure notes model, at the first paint (vinary.slides.notes · plan)|
start
:the evidence: the page labels, the Producer,
the page sizes (<latex>n</latex> pages), the second-screen axis;  <<IR_TINT>>
if (a second-screen axis\n(geometry, or pdfpc's notes position)?) then (yes)
  :split notes: every page is a slide half
  and a notes half (:style :split);  <<IR_TINT>>
  stop
elseif (not a Beamer source, or one page?) then (yes)
  :shown as it is (:not-beamer · :one-page);  <<IR_TINT>>
  stop
elseif (no page labels (one XeLaTeX pass)?) then (yes)
  if (<latex>n > 2000</latex> (max-content-pages)?) then (yes)
    :shown as it is (:too-many-pages),
    before any page is read;  <<IR_TINT>>
    stop
  else (no)
    :pending: the SCAN;  <<IR_TINT>>
  endif
elseif (a label that is not a canonical\nnon-negative integer?) then (yes)
  :shown as it is (:labels-not-integers);  <<IR_TINT>>
  stop
else (integer labels <latex>L_0, \dots, L_{n-1}</latex>)
  :**interleaving**(<latex>L</latex>): the gap decomposition,
  one pass (§2.1–§2.3);  <<IR_TINT>>
  if (status?) then (:proven — one valid parse)
    if (the Producer names pdfTeX, LuaTeX or LuaHBTeX,\nand <latex>L</latex> is not restartable (the guard, §2.4)?) then (yes)
      :hidden at once, proof [:labels]:
      no page is read;  <<IR_TINT>>
      note right ERROR_TINT
        §2.4: a restart deck whose appendix has
        a note page lands here with slides hidden:
        <latex>W(n)</latex> of the <latex>n</latex>-page decks that restart
        at 1. So does a counter set forward by
        hand (§4.6). Nothing reads a page to
        catch it.
      end note
      stop
    elseif (CONFIRM would read more than\n2000 distinct pages?) then (yes)
      :shown as it is (:too-many-pages);  <<IR_TINT>>
      stop
    else (no)
      :pending: CONFIRM;  <<IR_TINT>>
    endif
  elseif (status?) then (:ambiguous — the plain run branches)
    :pending: the PROBE (and CONFIRM after it
    unless the Producer writes its labels in the run);  <<IR_TINT>>
  else (:none · :invalid · :undecidable)
    :shown as it is (:no-note-pages ·
    :invalid · :undecidable);  <<IR_TINT>>
    stop
  endif
endif
|#E3F2ED|background, after the first paint (vinary.slides.evidence · settle, page text through pdf.js)|
:one page reader for the whole decision: it keeps 4 pages
and refuses the 2001st read (:too-many-pages, §4.5);  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
switch (pending?)
case (the SCAN)
  :read every page once, in order: page <latex>j</latex> is a note page
  when <latex>\mathrm{SIG}(s, j)</latex> holds for the last slide <latex>s</latex> (§4.4);  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
case (the PROBE)
  :walk the candidates from the last, reading <latex>(a-1, a)</latex>:
  it passes → candidate <latex>a</latex> · page <latex>a</latex> is dated → the previous
  candidate · otherwise → the parse without notes in the run (§4.1–§4.3);  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
  if (the Producer writes its labels in the run?) then (no)
    :CONFIRM the probe's choice (§5),
    proof [:labels :probe :confirm];  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
  else (yes)
    :the probe's choice stands,
    proof [:labels :probe];  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
    note right ERROR_TINT
      §4.6: with a frame counter set
      forward by hand, outside the rules,
      the probe can choose a parse that
      hides a slide, and no CONFIRM
      follows to catch it.
    end note
  endif
case (CONFIRM)
  :for each note page <latex>j</latex>, in order: <latex>\mathrm{SIG}(s, j)</latex> or
  ROTATED-DATE(<latex>j</latex>), <latex>s</latex> the slide before it · stop at
  the first page that fails (§5);  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
endswitch
:decided: the note pages leave the audience's sequence
(:style :interleaved), or the deck is shown as it is with its
reason (:no-note-pages · :probe-undecided · :confirm-failed ·
:too-many-pages · :unreadable · :error);  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
stop

legend right
  |= Colour |= Owner / meaning |
  |<#E67E22>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the pure notes model, at the first paint (vinary.slides.notes) — the model orange |
  |<#2D9574>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the background reader: page text through pdf.js (vinary.slides.evidence) |
  |<#E0211D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| a path that can hide a slide with no CONFIRM to catch it (§2.4, §4.6) |
  Rules are tried in order; the first that matches decides.
  "Shown as it is" hides no page: the audience sees every page.
endlegend
@enduml
